l-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOMURA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURABE KAORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTSUKI MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO ELECTRIC INDUSTRIES</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMURA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURABE, KAORU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSUKI, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO ELECTRIC INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOMURA OSAMU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MURABE KAORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OTSUKI MAKOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOMURA, OSAMU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MURABE, KAORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OTSUKI, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A long-life spindle motor bearing which can prevent a swing of shaft due to oscillation during rotation, a reduction in rotating accuracy and a contact between the shaft and a bearing, and provide a high rotating accuracy, wherein the shaft (11) and a sleeve (12) are inclined by an external energizing force relatively to each other to utilize a dynamic pressure produced on a bearing part when they are rotated relatively to each other, a cylindrical surface (C) in parallel with the axis of the sleeve (12) is provided at the center part of the sleeve (12) and two tapered parts (A) and (B) diverging toward the outside are provided at both end parts of the cylindrical surface (C) continued to these tapered parts (A) and (B) to produce a dynamic pressure between the tapered parts (A) and (B) at both end parts and the shaft (11), the inclinations of the tapered parts (A) and (B) are made identical to that of the shaft (11) and the lengths of the tapered parts (A) and (B) should desirably be 1/4 or more of the length of the sleeve (12), the same effect being enabled also by forming the sleeve (12), to the contrary, in cylindrical shape, and providing a flat part (e) and tapered parts (a) and (b) at the center and on both sides of the outer peripheral part of the shaft (11), respectively.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un moteur à axe à longue durée de vie qui permet d'empêcher le balancement de l'arbre sous l'effet des oscillations pendant la rotation, la baisse de la précision de rotation et le contact entre l'arbre et le roulement; il permet en outre d'obtenir une précision élevée de la rotation. L'arbre (11) et une gaine (12) sont inclinés l'un par rapport à l'autre par une force d'excitation extérieure, ce qui permet d'utiliser une pression dynamique produite dans la partie roulement lorsqu'ils pivotent l'un par rapport à l'autre. Une surface cylindrique (C) parallèle à l'axe de la gaine (12) est réalisée dans la partie centrale de la gaine (12), et deux parties coniques (A) et (B) divergeant vers l'extérieur sont aménagées dans les deux parties d'extrémité de la surface cylindrique (C) qui se prolonge vers lesdites parties coniques (A) et (B) de manière à créer une pression dynamique entre, d'une part, les parties coniques (A) et (B) dans les deux parties d'extrémité, et, d'autre part, l'arbre (11). L'inclinaison des parties coniques (A) et (B) est identique à celle de l'arbre (11), et leur longueur est égale à à ou plus de la longueur de la gaine (12). On atteint le même résultat en formant une gaine (12) de forme cylindrique et en réalisant une partie plate (e) et des parties coniques (a) et (b) au centre et des deux côtés de la partie périphérique extérieure de l'arbre (11), respectivement.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>